GoldLink's change to melonDS (UC11): the steady overworld's rooms drawn exactly. A room's own
orthographic matrix is tiny in 20.12 (HeartGold's: 32 and 43 for a pixel per world unit), so
every vertex and the pixel snap rounded to 1/32 of a pixel, differently at each step of the
camera: edges on a pixel's border (plant boxes, counters) flipped a pixel every few steps, and
the 0.77 down could not be rounded to an exact 0.75. Scaled by OrthoW like the overworld's
(the same picture and depth), it rounds to 1/2048 of a pixel.

Applied by build.rs to a copy of the submodule (which stays at upstream).

--- a/src/GPU3D.cpp	2026-11-13 20:04:54.853275463 -0500
+++ b/src/GPU3D.cpp	2026-11-13 20:41:17.508640718 -0500
@@ -2621,7 +2621,16 @@
         m[15] = (s32)std::lround(K * 4096);
     }
     else
-        memcpy(m, p, sizeof(m)); // a room: already orthographic, only snapped
+    {
+        // A room: already orthographic, only snapped. Its matrix is tiny in 20.12 (HeartGold's
+        // rooms: 32 and 43 for a pixel per unit), so each vertex and the snap round to 1/32 of a
+        // pixel, a little differently at every step of the camera: an edge on a pixel's border
+        // (a plant box's, a counter's) flipped to the next pixel every few steps. Scaled by
+        // OrthoW (w = OrthoW: the same picture and depth, x/w and z/w unchanged), as the
+        // overworld's, it rounds to 1/2048 of a pixel and the scale below can be made exact.
+        for (int i = 0; i < 16; i++)
+            m[i] = (s32)std::clamp<s64>((s64)p[i] * (s64)OrthoW, INT32_MIN, INT32_MAX);
+    }
     // A whole number of pixels for every step: the ground's scale on screen, per world unit
     // (along world x across the screen, along world z down it), rounded to a quarter pixel when
     // that's within 6% (HeartGold's field: 1.02 and 0.77, a tile 16 by 12 pixels). The player
